.com/story/geotab-adds-ai-powered-fatigue-detection-driver-coaching-tools-1fe359e985/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:35:03 +0000</pubDate><category>Drivers &amp; Jobs</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>Trucking Hub launches new platform for instant motor vehicle records</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/trucking-hub-launches-new-platform-for-instant-motor-vehicle-records-db9d583df8/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/trucking-hub-launches-new-platform-for-instant-motor-vehicle-records-db9d583df8/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:34:04 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>TheTrucker.com</description></item><item><title>Truck driver arrested after fatal Highway 30 collision that killed mother, son</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/truck-driver-arrested-after-fatal-highway-30-collision-that-killed-mot-103b0ffbb7/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/truck-driver-arrested-after-fatal-highway-30-collision-that-killed-mot-103b0ffbb7/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:29:42 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>CTV News</description></item><item><title>FMCSA seeks input on using cameras in place of truck mirrors</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/fmcsa-seeks-input-on-using-cameras-in-place-of-truck-mirrors-73eef295fa/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/fmcsa-seeks-input-on-using-cameras-in-place-of-truck-mirrors-73eef295fa/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:22:46 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>FMCSA has opened a public comment period on a request to let fleets use Safety Vision&#x27;s View Smart cameras instead of the two side mirrors required on commercial trucks and buses. A notice published Nov. 18 in the Federal Register says Safety Vision is seeking a five-year exemption from the rule requiring a rear-vision mirror on each side, and the agency has not approved the request. The system uses weatherproof cameras on both sides that feed video to screens mounted along the windshield, which the company says offers a wider view, better low-light visibility and alerts for nearby pedestrians or vehicles. Safety Vision has supplied the system to transit bus operators since 2024, though those buses still carry their required mirrors. FMCSA will weigh the application, safety analyses and public comments before deciding whether the system offers safety equal to conventional mirrors. Comments are accepted at Regulations.gov through Dec. 18 under docket FMCSA-2026-3707.</description></item><item><title>Workhorse expands Canadian dealer network with Ontario’s BDS Fleet Service</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/workhorse-expands-canadian-dealer-network-with-ontario-s-bds-fleet-ser-e312a26da7/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/workhorse-expands-canadian-dealer-network-with-ontario-s-bds-fleet-ser-e312a26da7/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:14:33 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>J.B. Hunt sees cost pressures ease, touts dedicated wins</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/j-b-hunt-sees-cost-pressures-ease-touts-dedicated-wins-f87d6a1439/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/j-b-hunt-sees-cost-pressures-ease-touts-dedicated-wins-f87d6a1439/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:27:51 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Canadian freight volumes climb as US spot rates remain elevated</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/canadian-freight-volumes-climb-as-us-spot-rates-remain-elevated-9d10911ef3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/canadian-freight-volumes-climb-as-us-spot-rates-remain-elevated-9d10911ef3/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:20:44 +0000</pubDate><category>Rates &amp; Market</category><description>Truck News</description></item