://haultimes.com/story/redwood-report-lists-9-warning-signs-for-shippers-picking-a-4pl-a5323e9a19/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/redwood-report-lists-9-warning-signs-for-shippers-picking-a-4pl-a5323e9a19/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Highway Trucking Strengthens On-Time Truckload and Expedited Freight Service for Ohio Shippers</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/highway-trucking-strengthens-on-time-truckload-and-expedited-freight-s-04cb36269d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/highway-trucking-strengthens-on-time-truckload-and-expedited-freight-s-04cb36269d/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:33:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>EIN News</description></item><item><title>Exception Management in Freight: How AI Is Changing the Work</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/exception-management-in-freight-how-ai-is-changing-the-work-478c487ccd/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/exception-management-in-freight-how-ai-is-changing-the-work-478c487ccd/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:04:58 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Transport Topics published a feature saying AI is taking over routine freight work, such as load entry and invoice processing, and shifting staff toward exception management. Under that model, automated systems handle routine work, and people step in when a delayed load or billing mismatch needs attention. The article cites industry surveys finding that more than 60% of logistics businesses use some form of AI.

The executives quoted describe assistants that support decisions and flag problems, while agents can act across platforms and resolve some exceptions, though they still need oversight. For companies starting out, the piece recommends beginning with one small, measurable project and expanding gradually once teams understand the tool.</description></item><item><title>Saia seeks exemption to allow CLP holders to pull doubles with supervision</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/saia-seeks-exemption-to-allow-clp-holders-to-pull-doubles-with-supervi-2de8a29ece/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/saia-seeks-exemption-to-allow-clp-holders-to-pull-doubles-with-supervi-2de8a29ece/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:01:39 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Commercial Carrier Journal</description></item><item><title>US Trucking Companies Targeted by Fake Carrier Verification Sites Stealing Passwords and Financial Data</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/us-trucking-companies-targeted-by-fake-carrier-verification-sites-stea-3600f5a667/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/us-trucking-companies-targeted-by-fake-carrier-verification-sites-stea-3600f5a667/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:27:52 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>GBHackers News</description></item><item><title>Shafaq News..Truck drivers, traders protest Mandali crossing closure</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/shafaq-news-truck-drivers-traders-protest-mandali-crossing-closure-7faacb4334/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/shafaq-news-truck-drivers-traders-protest-mandali-crossing-closure-7faacb4334/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 08:56:51 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>شفق نيوز</description></item><item><title>Oregon logging union calls on Kotek, lawmakers to address high diesel prices</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/oregon-logging-union-calls-on-kotek-lawmakers-to-address-high-diesel-p-88c5a6a00e/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/oregon-logging-union-calls-on-kotek-lawmakers-to-address-high-diesel-p-88c5a6a00e/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 08:00:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Fuel</category><description>KOIN.com</description></item><item><title>Hackers Impersonate Freight Booking Platforms to Deploy CastleRAT Malware on Trucking Companies’ Systems</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/hackers-impersonate-freight-booking-platforms-to-deploy-castlerat-malw-6a801321ec/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/hackers-impersonate-freight-booking-platforms-to-deploy-castlerat-malw-6a801321ec/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:01:16 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Cyber Press</description></item><item><title>Parts and Accessories Necessary for Safe Operation; Application for Exemption From Safety Vision, LLC</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/parts-and-accessories-necessary-for-safe-operation-application-for-exe-58ba138936/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/parts-and-accessories-necessary-for-safe-operation-application-for-exe-58ba138936/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:00:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>The Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration is asking for public comment on an exemption application from Safety Vision, LLC. The company wants to let motor carriers run commercial motor vehicles with its View Smart camera monitor system in place of the two rear-vision mirrors that the federal rules require. Safety Vision says the system offers an equivalent or greater level of safety, citing a wider field of view, better low-light performance, reduced blind spots and driver alerts. Comments are due December 18, 2026, under docket FMCSA-2026-3707. The notice does not signal what FMCSA will decide, and the agency will grant or deny the exemption after reviewing the application, safety analyses and public comments.</description></item><item><title>Commercial Driver&#x27;s License: Saia LTL Freight; Application for Exemption</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/commercial-driver-s-license-saia-ltl-freight-application-for-exemption-191ef37698/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/commercial-driver-s-license-saia-ltl-freight-application-for-exemption-191ef37698/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:00:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>The Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration is asking for public comment on an exemption application from Saia LTL Freight, a company headquartered in John Creek, Georgia. Saia wants commercial learner&#x27;s permit holders in its driver training program to operate combination vehicles with double trailers while under the direct supervision of a CDL holder with a doubles/triples endorsement. The notice states that it does not indicate what decision FMCSA will ultimately reach.

Saia has requested a 5-year exemption from two rules, 49 CFR 383.93(b)(1) and 383.37(a). According to the filing, approximately 300 trainees a year would use a fleet of about 19 training vehicles. Comments are due December 18, 2026, under docket FMCSA-2026-2642. After reviewing the application, safety analyses and public comments, FMCSA will either grant or deny the request.</description></item><item><title>Mack Makes Comparing Truck Configurations Easier</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/mack-makes-comparing-truck-configurations-easier-f1ddbaa71d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/mack-makes-comparing-truck-configurations-easier-f1ddbaa71d/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:40:29 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Mack Trucks has launched MyGarage, a free feature inside its online Truck Builder. Buyers can save, name, search and reopen multiple truck configurations, then send a saved build directly to a Mack dealer when they are ready to talk specifics. Users can also review truck images and selected specifications, and reopen a build to keep refining it. Separately, Truck Builder now lets customers add their company logo to a configured truck, a feature previously limited to Mack dealers.</description></item><item><title>FMCSA ELD Removals: 133 Devices and Fleet Checks</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/fmcsa-eld-removals-133-devices-and-fleet-checks-1ec12a7da7/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/fmcsa-eld-removals-133-devices-and-fleet-checks-1ec12a7da7/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:25:58 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>Tank Transport</description></item><item><title>Two owner-operators win new Peterbilt, Freightliner</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/two-owner-operators-win-new-peterbilt-freightliner-9237874185/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/two-owner-operators-win-new-peterbilt-freightliner-9237874185/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:59:42 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>www.overdriveonline.com</description></item><item><title>Ease Logistics looks to expand use of autonomous trucks</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/ease-logistics-looks-to-expand-use-of-autonomous-trucks-264f4195df/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/ease-logistics-looks-to-expand-use-of-autonomous-trucks-264f4195df/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:31:51 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Trucking Dive</description></item><item><title>Over 100 pounds of suspected cocaine found in truckload of lettuce at Blaine border crossing</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/over-100-pounds-of-suspected-cocaine-found-in-truckload-of-lettuce-at-8ab31682bc/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/over-100-pounds-of-suspected-cocaine-found-in-truckload-of-lettuce-at-8ab31682bc/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:23:50 +0000</pubDate><category>Cross-Border</category><description>My Bellingham Now</description></item></channel></rss>